{
 "id": "understand_interaction",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "feature_identity"
 ],
 "description": "Understand METERS + MOVERS by INTERACTING over frames (first slice). The agent's exploration IS the experiment: it moves each frame, so a meter's read-out falls (evidence for drain-per-move -> committed as a clock with a rate) and a mover's motion is observed relative to the avatar (toward=chase / away=flee / neither=drift -> committed behaviour). Evidence accrues on the durable Feature; commit when confident. Observation-over-time, not a one-shot reach.",
